## Still just ideas

None of these exist. They're here because the pattern is worth noticing: physical objects that display one fact, small devices that do one thing at a time.

- An e-ink display that hangs on the wall and fetches the front page of today's newspaper.
- A display that hangs on a window and identifies the planes going by, if you're standing in the right spot.
- A routine that runs OSMnx and PySRTM together to make a printable diorama of wherever you are.
- A display that shows which birds are audible right now.
- A synthesizer built on the M5Stack Cardputer.
- A little printer that prepares you for your day.
- A clock that counts down to the end of the current meeting, warming toward red as the end approaches.
- A physical button that Spotify-likes whatever is playing.
- A "stingray" detector, to notice when your cell tower is being spoofed and your connection quietly downgraded.
- A site to show off tee shirt designs.
- A URL compressor, as distinguished from a database-backed shortener.

Some of these will move up the page; others that sit here too long may get deleted.
